      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this will start blocking the main MDSal shared notification thread again, if the queue reaches 10 000 route-changes? This can happen if the peer is slower than we are - not dead, but slow.\n- Peer drains slowly\n- The bgp-adj-rib-out-\u003cpeer\u003e Thread parks in ChannelOutputLimiter.ensureWritable()\n- Routes keep flowing\n- The executor\u0027s single thread is not consuming, so the queue grows.\n- Queue reaches 10 000. The next executor.execute() falls through to caller-runs and parks the shared notification thread too.\n- The session stays up throughout, because the peer keeps sending keepalives in the other direction.\n- Nothing times out and clears the backlog.",
