      "message": "You are right, and it still blocks. With newCallerWaitsPolicy the executor blocks the submitting thread once the 10000 queue is full, so for a slow peer the shared notification thread can still park there.\n\nWhat the switch from the previous policy fixed is the reordering and the inline execution, not this.\nThe queue only fills for a peer that cannot keep up, so healthy peers are unaffected, but that is exactly the case you raised. The proper fix is to reset the peer when its queue fills, so it reconnects and resyncs instead of blocking.\n\nThat is a larger change, so I will prepare a separate task for it.",
